@HostAddress = http://localhost:5089

###

### Get all books
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Books
Accept: application/json

###

### Get book by id
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Books/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a book
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "category": "Software Engineering",
  "isAvailable": true
}

###

### Update a book (PUT)
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/Books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code (2nd Edition)",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "category": "Software Engineering",
  "isAvailable": false
}

###

### Partially update a book (PATCH)
PATCH {{HostAddress}}/api/Books/1
Content-Type: application/json-patch+json

[
  { "op": "replace", "path": "/isAvailable", "value": true }
]

###

### Delete a book
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/Books/1

###--- Loans Endpoint ---###

### 1. Get all loans
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get loan by id 
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. POST (Create) a New Loan
# Note: Id is omitted because the database auto-generates it. ReturnDate is omitted because the book is freshly borrowed.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 1,
  "memberId": 1,
  "borrowDate": "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z",
  "status": "Active"
}

### 4. PUT (Replace) a Loan
# Note: PUT requires the entire object to be sent to replace the existing record.
PUT {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 1,
  "memberId": 1,
  "borrowDate": "2026-08-13T00:00:00Z",
  "returnDate": "2026-08-20T00:00:00Z",
  "status": "Returned"
}

### 5. PATCH (Partial Update) a Loan
# Note: This uses JSON Patch syntax to update only specific fields (e.g., updating just the status).
PATCH {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans/1
Content-Type: application/json-patch+json

[
  {
    "op": "replace",
    "path": "/status",
    "value": "Overdue"
  }
]

### 6. DELETE a Loan
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/Loans/1